%S A399264 1,0,0,0,0,0,3,8,74,478,4576,49134,682541,11868102,265639155
%N A399264 Number of asymmetric connected bipartite graphs with n vertices.
%C A399264 For n >= 2, a connected bipartite graph has a unique bipartition, up to interchanging the two parts. For equal part sizes, automorphisms interchanging the two parts must also be excluded.
%D A399264 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, New York, 1973.
%D A399264 V. Jovovic, Symmetry Types of Combinatorial Structures, manuscript, 2026.
%H A399264 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A399264/a399264.pdf">Computation of Asymmetric Connected Bipartite Graphs</a>
%H A399264 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A399264/a399264_1.pdf">Illustrations of Asymmetric Connected Bipartite Graphs</a>
%F A399264 Let b(p,q) be the number of connected asymmetric bipartite graphs with bipartition sizes p and q, counted up to isomorphism. Then a(n) = Sum_{1 <= p <= q, p+q=n} b(p,q).
%e A399264 a(7) = 3: there are 3 nonisomorphic connected bipartite graphs on 7 vertices with trivial automorphism group.
%Y A399264 Cf. A005142 (connected bipartite graphs), A124059 (connected asymmetric graphs).
%K A399264 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A399264 1,7
%A A399264 _Vladeta Jovovic_, Aug 25 2026
